  "asr_text": "Participants who were strongly inclined to enjoy seeing others suffer were more likely to reduce the other person's reward after watching the stone video than after watching the magician video. Among those with a weaker tendency, there was no clear difference. You might want to dismiss this by saying, so it really is a matter of personality, but there's more to the story. In the next experiment, participants were again randomly assigned to groups, but this time there was no option to increase the reward. The only choice was to reduce it. This time, regardless of how strongly participants were inclined to enjoy seeing others suffer, those who watched the stone video were more likely to reduce another person's reward than those in the other conditions. Well, if we focus only on personality, we may miss something. Along with what kind of person someone is, there's also what they can do in that situation. We thought we were reading a profile of the person, but now we start noticing the stage setup too.",
